{"text": "Tranter & Holroyd Chartered Accountants - IHT WORKSHEET - file RAM/E/0418\nDeceased: Edith Maud Ramsbottom (\"Edie\")        Prepared NT, 7 Nov 2025\n\nDate of birth 11 October 1928.  Date of death 28 August 2025, aged 96, at home.\nLast address: 17 Whalley Old Road, Clitheroe, Lancashire BB7 1NB\nNI no. ZH 20 44 18 C     UTR 44187 72093     HMRC IHT ref (applied for 3/10/25): A418772/25K\nWidow of Harold (d. 2009) - his unused nil rate band is available in full; grant and his will located.\nExecutors: son Clive Ramsbottom (01632 960141) and granddaughter Philippa Entwhistle-Shaw (07700 900177, pippa.es@pendlemail.example).\nSolicitors on the grant: Ribble & Hodder Solicitors, ref RH/PRB/2204. We do the IHT400 and schedules only.\n\nASSETS AT DATE OF DEATH                                                          £\n House, Whalley Old Road (two valuations, mid-point)                       285,000\n Calderbrook Building Society  sort 60-44-18  a/c 20441877  (current)        14,206.31\n Calderbrook cash ISA  a/c 70018442                                      62,480.00\n NS&I Premium Bonds, holder no. 2204418A                                     30,000\n Spanish account kept from the flat she sold in 2016:\n   Caja Levantina del Mediterráneo, Torrevieja  IBAN ES32 6635 7455 4445 2071 4812\n   EUR 18,442.10 at death = £15,871 at the day's rate (IHT417 not needed; put on IHT400 box for foreign assets)\n Teachers' pension arrears to date of death                                    1,104.66\n Car, 2014 Honda Jazz, reg PK14 XTD (sold to a neighbour)                       3,200\n Contents / jewellery (probate valuation)                                      4,750\nLIABILITIES\n Funeral (Clive paid on his own card, to be reimbursed)                            (4,312.00)\n Care agency final invoice CA-118204                                         (1,846.50)\n\nLIFETIME GIFTS IN THE 7 YEARS (IHT403) - from her cheque stubs and what the family told us\n 14 Feb 2020    £40,000 to Clive \"for the extension\"            -> more than 5 yrs, taper applies if tax were due\n Christmas 2022   £3,000 each to four great-grandchildren -> annual exemptions 2022/23 + b/f\n 2 May 2024     £25,000 to Pippa for her house deposit          -> chargeable, within nil rate band\n Monthly £250 standing order to her grandson Mark, who the family say has a gambling problem\n   since June 2021 -> claim as normal expenditure out of income; need 3 yrs of her income figures. Clive would\n   rather this was left off. Told him it cannot be.\n\nPOINTS\n - Estate about £410,000 net before gifts; with both nil rate bands and residence nil rate band (house to direct descendants) no tax expected, but the full IHT400 is needed because of the foreign asset and the gifts.\n - Capacity: GP letter of March 2024 says early vascular dementia. The £25,000 gift was made two months later. If Clive challenges it, that is for the solicitors, not us.\n - Edie was a lifelong Methodist; will leaves £5,000 to the chapel (charity exemption, IHT408 not required).\n - Our fee: £1,950 + VAT, agreed with both executors 31/10/2025.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "446 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Edith Maud Ramsbottom", "Harold", "Clive Ramsbottom", "Philippa Entwhistle-Shaw", "Mark", "Clive", "Edie"], "companies": ["Tranter & Holroyd Chartered Accountants", "Calderbrook Building Society", "Calderbrook cash ISA", "Ribble & Hodder Solicitors", "Caja Levantina del Mediterráneo", "Honda", "Methodist"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Clitheroe", "Whalley Old Road", "Torrevieja"], "health": ["vascular dementia"], "sensitive": ["Clive", "Philippa Entwhistle-Shaw", "Harold", "Mark"], "names": ["Edith", "Harold", "Clive", "Philippa", "Mark", "Edie"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.10000000149011612, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban"